# 03 - Linux Endpoint and Agent Setup

## Objective

Create a monitored Linux endpoint and install the Wazuh agent for centralized log collection.

## VM Specifications

| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| Name | Linux-Endpoint |
| RAM | 1024-1536 MB |
| CPU | 1 core |
| Disk | 25 GB |
| Network | Shared Network |
| Hostname | linux-endpoint |

## Ubuntu Server Installation

Follow standard Ubuntu Server ARM64 installation.

Enable OpenSSH server during installation.

## Network Verification

```bash
ip addr
```

Record the IP address. Example:

```text
Linux-Endpoint IP: 192.168.64.14
```

## System Update

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade -y
```

## Install Basic Tools

```bash
sudo apt install -y curl wget net-tools htop vim ufw auditd
```

## Enable SSH

Verify SSH is running:

```bash
sudo systemctl status ssh
```

If not running:

```bash
sudo apt install -y openssh-server
sudo systemctl enable ssh
sudo systemctl start ssh
```

## Enable UFW Firewall

```bash
sudo ufw allow ssh
sudo ufw enable
sudo ufw status verbose
```

## Install Wazuh Agent

In the Wazuh dashboard:

1. Go to Agents
2. Select Deploy new agent
3. Choose Linux / DEB / ARM64
4. Enter SOC-SIEM IP as manager address
5. Copy the installation command

Run the command on Linux-Endpoint, then start the agent:

```bash
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable wazuh-agent
sudo systemctl start wazuh-agent
sudo systemctl status wazuh-agent
```

## Verification

In Wazuh dashboard:

- Confirm `linux-endpoint` appears
- Confirm status is Active

